      "message": "`SkImageShader::MakeSubset` used to only be called from code internal to ganesh or graphite (as part of image filtering, where the images involved were already matching the backend).\n\nWith the auto-mask-filter path, MakeSubset is being called with raster images before graphite/ganesh have had a chance to upload them. This is fine, since only graphite uses the auto-mask-filter path for now, and the `appendStages` function for SkImageShader has an equivalent assert that makes sure we never try to use a subset image shader on a non-gpu backend.",
